  "concept": {
    "biome": "reedstrand_delta_marsh",
    "recommendedLevelRange": [
      24,
      40
    ],
    "skyPreset": "golden_alpine_meadow",
    "loreSummary": "Turf that burns and water that is not salt. Reedstrand's eight regions draw no rock, no scree and no karst between them, so the only stone on this head is what the sea has broken off its own platform and laid along the raised beach \u2014 and there is nowhere near enough of it to quarry. What the head does have is peat in four separate mires and a spring line at the back of the fen. One region borders this one and no road is drawn anywhere on the landmass, so a crew comes in off the water, cuts, and goes back out the way it came."
  },
